From: atjiki1 <atjiki1@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 21:45:27 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/8] bt: pair and reconnect a secondary device

With CONFIG_BT_MULTI_LINK_EXPERIMENT:

- Settings > Bluetooth turns on secondary pairing while open. A new,
  unbonded device that connects then while a phone is bonded is treated
  as the secondary device: the watch sends a Security Request so it
  pairs, and the pairing is no longer rejected on a second link.
- Links are tracked as primary (phone), secondary or extra. Only the
  primary drives legacy connection events and "connected as slave".
- Advertising for the secondary runs while it is bonded and not
  connected, also while the phone is connected. After a link comes up,
  the remaining advertising jobs are restarted while another link can
  still be accepted.
- Forgetting the secondary while connected drops its link.
- The settings hint explains how to add a second device.
- bonding.c reports the role the storage chose to the connection.

Add pbl_bt_gap_le_security_initiate() to the NimBLE glue.

Assisted-by: LLM
